<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Asturienne 1996 profit up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian Asturienne 1996 profit up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		314  vs  277</p>
<p>    Minorities			127  vs   76</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		 441  vs  353</p>
<p>    Dividend (francs)		43  vs   41</p>
<p>    Cons current profit	   587  vs  506</p>
<p>    Cons operating profit	 534  vs  454</p>
<p>    of which mica businesses    144  vs  147</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;  industrial minerals   107  vs  152</p>
<p>&quot;  &quot;  lead and silver mines 307  vs  171</p>
<p>NOTE - Cie Royale Asturienne des Mines is a Belgian mining company controlled ultimately by Switzerland's Harwanne group.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
